<newsitem itemid="356616" id="root" date="1997-02-05" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Eagle yr headline shr jumps, div increased.</title>
<headline>Eagle yr headline shr jumps, div increased.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		     860.8     vs    413.3</p>
<p>    - attrib		     1,257.4     vs    1,510.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)			350.0     vs    250.0</p>
<p>    Net attrib. income	  153.15     vs    184.01</p>
<p>    Gross written premium   1,561.00     vs    1,461.09</p>
<p>    Underwriting profit	  22.33     vs    23.04 loss</p>
<p>    Investment income	   133.37     vs    95.57</p>
<p>Surplus on</p>
<p>    disposal of items	    42.96     vs    143.36</p>
<p>Div payable March 20</p>
<p>On register March 7</p>
<p>Full name: South African Eagle Insurance Company Ltd (insurance)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said all accounts performed well except the fire account which was adversely affected by claims in excess of 25 million rand relating to the extreme weather conditions in the first quarter of 1996. It said the account continued to be problematic due to inadequate market ratings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
